      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the **Guarded Write Journal** provides rollback capability for file writes in Grimoire\u0027s agent runtime.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n1. **Pre-write recording**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory journal.\n\n2. **Rollback mechanism**: If an agent run fails (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal rolls back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n\n3. **Transaction semantics**: This approach provides all-or-nothing write semantics without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the in-memory journal itself acts as the transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\n4. **Query agent exemption**: The Query agent doesn\u0027t use this rollback functionality because it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library.",
